            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Hindi for cancer, then the Hindi for to stiffen."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: तीमारदारी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तीमारदारी — tīmārdārī — \"nursing the sick\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बीमारी में मीरा ने अपनी माँ की बहुत तीमारदारी की। bīmārī meṁ Mīrā ne apnī māṁ kī bahut tīmārdārī kī. Mira nursed her mother devotedly through her illness."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "तीमारदारी (tīmārdārī) is usually traced to Persian tīmārdārī, \"tending the sick\", built on tīmār, \"care of the sick\", and -dārī, \"keeping\". tīmārdār is the person at the bedside."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
