          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "लिटाना (liṭānā) is the causative partner of leṭnā, \"to lie down\", which CDIAL lists under Sanskrit lēṭyáti (CDIAL 11109); the vowel shortens before the causative ending."
